Author: Portos (Yishan) Wang [aut, cre], Bingxin Cai [aut]
Maintainer: Portos (Yishan) Wang <portos.wang@gmail.com>
Description: A comprehensive tool for calculating sample sizes across
    various clinical study designs. Provides a three-axis application
    programming interface (design, statistical task, and outcome type)
    covering experimental trials (superiority, non-inferiority,
    equivalence), observational studies (cohort, case-control,
    cross-sectional), diagnostic accuracy studies (sensitivity and
    specificity estimation and comparison, area under the receiver
    operating characteristic curve, likelihood ratios), and complex
    designs (cluster randomised trials, two-stage phase II designs,
    bioequivalence, ordered categorical outcomes). Each calculation
    returns the formula, parameter-role documentation, and precise
    literature citations with section-level detail. Built following
    tidy design principles with comprehensive parameter validation and
    structured error handling.
